  "id": "winner-effect",
  "term": "winner effect",
  "definition": "The winner effect is a short-lived increase in aggressive motivation or behavior after an individual wins a fight or other competitive encounter. In the supplied source, repeated recent wins made later fights more intense and longer, suggesting that the experience of winning can temporarily heighten aggressiveness.",
